      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a48d248ef60073948d92",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>The kernel-api no longer has a direct dependency on JCR, so in principle, there is no blocker for this ticket.</p>\n\n<p>That said, my original point in opening this ticket was predicated on the idea that the HTTP-* modules could be re-used in an alternate Fedora implementation. I no longer see that as a possibility, and so from my perspective the benefit/utility of reworking the unit test mocks is quite limited.</p>",
     "created": "09/Feb/17 9:48 AM",
     "id": "18545",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/12209/comment/18545",
